config UMS9117_NANDC_RO
	bool "UMS9117 read-only internal NAND"
	depends on ARCH_UMS9117 && HAS_DMA && !MTD
	help
	  Expose a physical stream containing every NAND page's main and OOB
	  bytes. The first open identifies the fitted SPI NAND from its ID
	  bytes. Supported chips have 2048-byte pages, 64 pages per block, 1024
	  blocks and one plane: FM25LG01B, DS35M1GA, GD5F1GQ4RExxG,
	  GD5F1GQ5RExxG, GD5F1GM7RExxG, GD5F1GQ5RExxH, F50D1G41LB and
	  MX35UF1G14AC. Reads from other chips are refused. Hardware is
	  activated only for explicit opens and reads; each read checks the
	  identity and feature state before returning data. No MTD, generic SPI
	  NAND, ioctl, mmap, feature-write, program or erase operation is
	  provided. The separate ADI SPI controller can coexist with this
	  reader.
